  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds access in Proxy-Protocol v1 header\n     parsing with an attacker-controlled proxy\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-94054.patch: set ret to the length of the\n       heap copy of the PROXY v1 line instead of adding the\n       swallow_until_crlf() count, so the memchr() for the CR stays\n       inside the copy\n     - CVE-2026-94054\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: uninitialised stack data read on a short\n     Proxy-Protocol v2 header from an attacker-controlled proxy\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-94056.patch: repeat the read of the v2\n       length fields until all 16 header octets have arrived, and abort\n       on EOF or error instead of using uninitialised length data\n     - CVE-2026-94056",
